 {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent production release that was healthy is v2.3.0. v2.3.1 is unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc only ran in staging. I'll roll back to v2.3.0, which has already been healthy in production, so no change-manager approval is needed.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01EdHHaQif3iBwehkvWxESNs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The rollback is verified. I'll confirm the service has recovered before opening the incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Pgipoj4CaV5FGX1tdmxNpo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01EsdrJdz8gJZxGDwRdgwzgE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after v2.3.1 was deployed to production (error rate was 0.18). I rolled production back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The rollback was verified. Service is now healthy on v2.3.0 with an error rate of 0.002. v2.3.1 remains unhealthy in production and should not be redeployed until it is fixed. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and confirm the root cause.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** It is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 is unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc was only deployed to staging.\n- **Result:** The rollback is verified. The service is healthy on v2.3.0 with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18 on v2.3.1.\n- **Approval:** No change-manager approval was needed, because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback, and the current state. It also notes that v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until it is fixed. The root cause is still open and needs follow-up.", "type": "text"}]}]}